name,n_o_material,n_e_material,reference,notes,gyration_deg_per_mm,gyration_ref_nm,gyration_reference
calcite,calcite_o,calcite_e,"Ghosh 1999, Opt. Commun. 163, 95-102; Bloss 1961/Hartshorne & Stuart classic mineralogy references for walk-off convention","negative uniaxial (n_e<n_o at all visible wavelengths: n_o(590nm)=1.658 > n_e(590nm)=1.486, delta_n=-0.172); walk-off angle rho=atan[(n_o/n_e)^2 * tan(theta)] - theta, max walk-off ~6.2 deg occurs near internal angle theta~45 deg from optic axis at 590nm; classic Nicol/Glan-Thompson prism and beam-displacer material"
quartz,quartz_o,quartz_e,"Ghosh 1999, Opt. Commun. 163, 95-102","positive uniaxial (n_e>n_o at all visible wavelengths: n_o(589nm)=1.5443 < n_e(589nm)=1.5534, delta_n=+0.0091); birefringence ~19x weaker than calcite so walk-off is correspondingly small (walk-off ~0.34 deg at theta=45 deg internal angle at 589nm, computed from rho=atan[(n_o/n_e)^2*tan(theta)]-theta); standard waveplate/retarder material (quartz order-sorting filters, Babinet-Soleil compensators)",21.77,589.3,"alpha-quartz rotatory power (specific rotation) along the optic axis at the sodium-D line 589.3 nm; classical value ~21.7-21.8 deg/mm (Kaminsky, Rep. Prog. Phys. 63, 1575 (2000); gyration tensor g33 also in Hoffman et al., Appl. Opt. 48, 5307 (2009)). Sign = right-handed (dextrorotatory) alpha-quartz. Berreman gyration scalar G = n_o*lam*rho/pi is derived from this in berreman.gyration_from_rotatory_power."
sapphire,sapphire_o,sapphire_e,"Malitson & Dodge 1972 (Al2O3 o-ray and e-ray Sellmeier), as tabulated by refractiveindex.info","negative uniaxial (n_e<n_o: n_o(589nm)=1.7682 > n_e(589nm)=1.7600, delta_n=-0.0082); weak birefringence similar in magnitude to quartz, so walk-off is small (walk-off ~0.27 deg at theta=45 deg internal angle at 589nm, computed from rho=atan[(n_o/n_e)^2*tan(theta)]-theta using n_o=1.7682,n_e=1.7600); used for durable c-axis windows/waveplates where quartz is too soft or not thermally/chemically robust enough"
linbo3,linbo3_o,linbo3_e,Zelmon Small & Jundt 1997 JOSA B 14 3319,NEGATIVE uniaxial congruent LiNbO3; dn=-0.084@633; walk-off ~2.1deg@45deg; EO/QPM workhorse (chi2 needs engine support)
litao3,litao3_o,litao3_e,Bond 1965 J. Appl. Phys. 36 1674 (tabulated); Sellmeier fit ours,"POSITIVE uniaxial, tiny dn~+0.004; index rows are fits (composition UNVERIFIED); walk-off <0.3deg"
yvo4,yvo4_o,yvo4_e,Shi Zhang & Shen 2001 J. Synth. Cryst. 30 85,"POSITIVE uniaxial, LARGE dn=+0.223@633; walk-off ~5deg@45; isolator/displacer/Wollaston material"
bbo,bbo_o,bbo_e,Tamosauskas et al. 2018 Opt. Mater. Express 8 1410,NEGATIVE uniaxial beta-BBO; dn=-0.112@1064; premier UV SHG/OPO crystal (chi2 needs engine support)
alpha_bbo,abbo_o,abbo_e,UNVERIFIED (CASTECH-lineage vendor Sellmeier),NEGATIVE uniaxial alpha-BBO polarizer phase; |dn|~0.12; INDEX ROWS UNVERIFIED (vendor sources disagree >1e-3)
kdp,kdp_o,kdp_e,Zernike 1964 JOSA 54 1215,NEGATIVE uniaxial dn=-0.042@532; EO Pockels/frequency-doubling; hygroscopic
adp,adp_o,adp_e,Zernike 1964 JOSA 54 1215,NEGATIVE uniaxial dn=-0.046@532; KDP isomorph
rutile,rutile_o,rutile_e,DeVore 1951 JOSA 41 416,POSITIVE uniaxial VERY LARGE dn=+0.288@633; polarizer/walk-off material; ABSORBS below ~0.43um (needs UV k)
teo2,teo2_o,teo2_e,Uchida 1971 Phys. Rev. B 4 3736,POSITIVE uniaxial dn=+0.152@633; paratellurite acousto-optic (AOTF/AOM) workhorse; valid 0.4-1.0um
mgf2,mgf2,mgf2_e,Dodge 1984 Appl. Opt. 23 1980,POSITIVE uniaxial dn=+0.012; n_o = existing 'mgf2' row; adds e-ray so MgF2 waveplates/Rochon prisms work
